   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "How the reference pictures align with the target video \u2014 Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 4.46-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, realistic UGC iPhone selfie video, vertical 9:16, one continuous handheld front-camera take with a subtle natural sway, small arm micro-jitters, autofocus gently re-focusing and natural exposure shifts. Real unretouched skin with visible pores, fine lines and natural shine, flyaway hairs and mild phone-camera noise. The shot begins in the position and framing established by Picture 1: a warm, relatable American woman in her fifties, with shoulder-length brown hair worn down and a soft blue cardigan, in her bright kitchen in soft morning light, standing at the counter. A plain white unlabeled pill jar stands on the counter in front of her, in the lower right of the frame. Her phone hand stretches toward the lens at the lower left edge of the frame; that phone is the camera. Her free hand rests on the counter beside the jar. [0.2s-1.1s] Her free hand closes around the jar and lifts it a few inches off the counter. [1.1s-2.1s] She gives the jar one short, hard shake. [2.1s-3.0s] She sets the jar back down on the counter in the same spot. [3.0s-4.0s] She opens her fingers and lays her hand flat on the counter beside the jar. [4.0s-4.5s] She looks into the lens with a dry, serious face, her lips together, her free hand resting on the counter beside the jar, settling into the pose, spacing and framing established by Picture 2. Her face stays tired and serious throughout. Outside the moments described above, her lips stay gently closed and relaxed. The woman stays the same person with natural hands for the whole shot, and everything important stays in the center of the frame.\n\noverall_soundscape: Close iPhone microphone audio, quiet kitchen room tone in the morning.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
   ],
   "title": "PROMPT \u00b7 take 2 in MiniMax's format (`take_graph.py --print-prompt`)",
   "color": "#223",
   "bgcolor": "#335"
  },
